# PROP-108: TLS termination for the LiveKit signaling WebSocket.
#
# LiveKit's WebRTC media transport is already encrypted by default
# (DTLS-SRTP, inherent to the protocol -- see ../observability/SECURITY_AUDIT.md
# section 5) regardless of this file. What's NOT encrypted without this:
# the signaling WebSocket itself, which livekit-server serves as plain
# ws:// on :7880 (see docker-compose.yml). Caddy terminates real TLS here
# (automatic Let's Encrypt cert + renewal, zero extra config) and proxies
# to that same port, turning ws://<vm-ip>:7880 into wss://<domain>:443 --
# Caddy's reverse_proxy handles WebSocket upgrades transparently, no
# special directive needed.
#
# Requires a real domain name with a DNS A record pointing at the VM's
# static IP (reserved by ../gcp/provision_vm.sh) -- the one piece of this
# that can't be built or tested without an actual deployed VM. Once that
# DNS record exists, set LIVEKIT_DOMAIN and this Just Works.

{$LIVEKIT_DOMAIN} {
	reverse_proxy localhost:7880
}
